import { auditHelperBase } from './lane-exports-rpc-ai-auth-audit-paths.mjs';
import { assertAuditOpen } from './lane-exports-rpc-ai-auth-completion-guard.mjs';
assertAuditOpen();
// Authored directly from complete source and regression-test reads; no delegation.
import fs from 'node:fs';
import path from 'node:path';
const base=auditHelperBase;
const root='/home/mewtwo/Zks/ice';
const main='packages/coding-agent/src/ice-safe-verify.ts';
const host='packages/coding-agent/src/ice-goals-host.ts';
const test='packages/coding-agent/test/ice-safe-verify.test.ts';
const htest='packages/coding-agent/test/ice-goals-host.test.ts';
const src=(p,a,b)=>'ice:'+p+':'+a+'-'+b;
const ref=(a,b)=>src(main,a,b);
const tests=(a,b)=>src(test,a,b);
const quote=(p,a,b)=>'```ts\n'+fs.readFileSync(path.join(root,p),'utf8').split('\n').slice(a-1,b).join('\n')+'\n```\nSource: '+src(p,a,b)+'.';
const genericRust='Rust has generic before/after-tool hooks (rust:crates/ice-agent/src/hooks.rs:29-130), active-tool/model/session actions (rust:crates/ice-extensions/src/actions.rs:381-499,881-923), and UI dialog mailboxes (same file:99-360). These are usable primitives, not an implementation of this policy. The complete Rust .rs search for guarded-plan state, draft_plan/read_plan/propose_plan, mutation_generation and ice.goals.host found no implementation; plan_mode_start/plan_mode_complete hits are transcript/widget rendering, not authority enforcement.';
const entries=[];
function add(n,title,priority,size,source,what,mechanism,interfaces,deps,rust,port,reason){entries.push({id:'SAFE-'+String(n).padStart(3,'0'),title,status:'missing',priority,size_min:size[0],size_max:size[1],source,what,mechanism,interfaces,dependencies:deps,rust,port,priority_reason:reason});}
add(1,'Mandatory guard bootstrap and process-scoped flags','P0',[120,220],
 src('packages/coding-agent/src/ice.ts',64,129)+'; '+ref(232,291)+'; '+ref(834,858)+'. Exported validateIceStartupArgs, parseIceMode, createIceSafeVerify; default iceSafeVerify. Tests: '+tests(51,112)+'.',
 'The ICE launcher starts in plan mode unless an explicit current-process flag or valid same-root session state selects build. Disabling user extensions does not disable the bundled guard.',
 'The launcher normalizes unsafe subagent flags first, then validates ICE flags, and on either error writes the error message to stderr and exits 1. It supplies ice-safe-verify as a hidden before-user factory, ahead of provider settings, Cognee and subagents. It maintains current mode and the last frozen capability snapshot for subagent admission. Stock cli.ts is intentionally a different launcher, without this factory; the regression explicitly distinguishes them.\n\nparseIceMode(undefined) returns plan; only exact plan/build strings are accepted. Startup rejects duplicate --ice-mode and duplicate --allow-external whether separate or equals syntax. --allow-external accepts only a bare flag or literal =true, requires explicit --ice-mode build, and rejects --no-approve, -na and --no-approve=anything. The validator scans --ice-verify through SAFE-019. Plan/build model references must be nonempty after trimming; the separate-value precheck does not reject a next token beginning with a dash. No duplicate checks exist here for verifier/model flags; do not invent them. Process opt-ins are reread from the extension flag registry on restore and mode changes, never restored as granted authority from a session. Sub-yolo terminal requirements belong to the preceding subagent normalizer, not this validator.',
 '| Flag | Type | Default/effect |\n|---|---|---|\n| --ice-mode | string | plan absent valid restored mode; exact plan or build |\n| --ice-allow-bash | boolean | false; effective only trusted build |\n| --allow-external | boolean | false; effective only trusted build; explicit startup build required |\n| --ice-verify | JSON argv string | absent; SAFE-019 |\n| --ice-workgraph-dispatch | boolean | false; declaration of intent, not coordinator startup |\n| --ice-plan-model | string | absent; scoped model resolution in SAFE-007 |\n| --ice-build-model | string | absent; execution model fallback in SAFE-007 |\n\nNo guard settings keys, environment-variable reads, keybindings or new RPC commands. Launcher environment writes and other startup flags are specified in cli-packaging.md.',
 ['SAFE-003','SAFE-004','SAFE-019','SAFE-025'],
 'rust:crates/ice-cli/src/args.rs:107-230,271-545 has no guard fields or validator; unknown long flags are merely retained at 511-524. Generic flags do not cause guard registration. '+genericRust,
 'Place bootstrap and CLI validation in ice-cli; place durable guard service in ice-harness. Always register it before optional plugins. Keep the stock-launcher distinction explicit rather than pretending every CLI entry point has the same policy. Host additions: process-scoped extension flag lookup and ordered mandatory registration. No external binary for validation.',
 'Without mandatory bootstrap, every later protection can be bypassed by selecting startup options.');
add(2,'Canonical guarded root and immutable Git baseline','P0',[80,160],
 ref(322,363)+'; '+ref(740,762)+'; '+ref(1825,1857)+'. Exported resolveProspectivePath/pathIsWithin; private captureBaseline/canonicalizeExisting. Tests: '+tests(125,167)+' and '+tests(149,155)+'; same-root restoration: '+tests(1452,1495)+'.',
 'A session has one guarded root and a baseline of the repository at first initialization. Resuming a matching branch state preserves its original baseline rather than silently rebasing it.',
 'Run git rev-parse --show-toplevel at ctx.cwd. Use trimmed stdout only on exit code 0; otherwise use cwd. Canonicalize with realpathSync, falling back to resolve on failure. At that root run rev-parse HEAD, branch --show-current, and status --porcelain=v1 -uall concurrently. Record optional head and nonempty branch only on code 0, raw porcelain stdout on code 0 otherwise empty string, and new Date().toISOString(). rootSource is git only if the root query produced a nonempty root. A thrown exec error is not caught by captureBaseline; nonzero exit is handled, thrown spawn errors propagate through restore.\n\nRestore increments a session epoch before asynchronous baseline capture. If another restore/shutdown changes the epoch before capture completes, discard the old restore. A valid saved state must match the newly canonicalized root exactly. For a valid match, use saved baseline but current rootSource; otherwise initialize a fresh baseline and zero generations. Baseline is evidence only: it does not lock Git or prevent external edits.',
 quote(main,161,167)+'\nFile persistence is the custom session record in SAFE-003, not a separate baseline file. External binary: git with the exact four argument vectors above. No model tool, CLI option beyond SAFE-001, env key, setting, slash command or keybinding.',
 ['SAFE-003'],
 'rust:crates/ice-cli/src/trust.rs:165-181 normalizes trust-store paths lexically; it does not capture this baseline. rust:crates/ice-tools/src/path_utils.rs:41-49 resolves tool paths but does not establish a guard root. Neither mechanism is equivalent to a persisted Git baseline.',
 'Implement a guard-root value object in ice-harness using std::fs canonicalization and tokio::process::Command for read-only Git probes. Preserve canonical-vs-lexical distinction, Windows comparison behavior, nonzero-exit fallbacks and restore epoch ordering. Do not reuse trust-store normalization as canonical root identity.',
 'Root identity is required before applying mutation and verification policy.');
add(3,'Version 3 durable guard state and branch restoration','P0',[240,420],
 ref(146,208)+'; '+ref(407,415)+'; '+ref(632,738)+'; '+ref(860,862)+'; '+ref(1825,1894)+'; '+src('packages/coding-agent/src/core/legacy-compat/identity.ts',1,3)+'. Symbols IcePlanState, IceVerifierState, IceGitBaseline, private IceStateV3/parseStoredState/parseStoredPlan/restore. Tests: '+tests(1100,1141)+'; '+tests(1432,1495)+'.',
 'Plan drafts, approvals, read acknowledgements, mutation counters and verification evidence survive session resume and branch navigation; process-only authority does not.',
 'Append the complete state with appendEntry("ice-safe-verify-state", state) at each persistence boundary. On session_start/session_tree, read only the current session branch, reverse it and select the latest custom entry whose customType exactly equals that string. The legacy-named matchesEntryType helper currently performs exact equality, not alias migration. Do not search earlier records when the newest matching record is invalid: warn "Ignored invalid ICE state entry." and initialize fresh state.\n\nAccept versions 1, 2 or 3; exact mode plan/build; exact guardRoot and baseline.root; rootSource git/cwd; nonnegative safe-integer mutation/checked counters with checked <= mutation; existing verifier object with a known status. Version 1 gets an empty plan. Versions 2/3 require parseStoredPlan: known status, boolean readInBuild; none requires false and resets other plan fields through emptyPlanState. Other statuses require title/markdown/hash strings; reminder count defaults 0 and must be a safe integer 0..3. Optional approval policy, timestamps, model strings and thinking enum are validated. Timestamps are nonnegative safe integers. Validate bounded/NUL-free title and Markdown; require already-trimmed title and exact SHA-256(JSON.stringify({title,markdown})). The parser does not deeply validate every baseline/verifier optional member; Rust strict decoding must not silently claim identical acceptance.\n\nEmit version 3 on restore. Explicit current --ice-mode overrides saved mode; otherwise saved mode then plan. A current verifier hash differing from saved produces pending with current hash; absent saved verifier produces pending if configured else not-configured; saved running becomes cancelled with "Previous verifier was interrupted before completion". Other saved statuses are retained, even when the current process has no verifier. checkedGeneration is not reset merely because command hash changed; automatic verification still uses the generation comparison. readInBuild survives a same-root resume, including an explicit build startup; it is reset by setMode(build) and session_compact instead. Clear in-flight authorized tool IDs on restore. Recompute bashEnabledInRecordedProcess from current flags/trust; never replay its saved true value.',
 quote(main,169,208)+'\nVerifier status enum: not-configured, pending, running, passed, failed, timed-out, spawn-error, cancelled, blocked-untrusted. Plan status: none/draft/pending/approved. Plan context policy: fresh/compact/keep. Thinking accepted by this parser: off/minimal/low/medium/high/xhigh/max/ultra. The state is JSON data inside a session custom entry; session-file placement/atomic append semantics are owned by the session subsystem. No standalone ~/.ice guard file.',
 ['SAFE-002','SAFE-019'],
 'Generic append/session-branch actions exist at rust:crates/ice-extensions/src/actions.rs:393-499,881-923, but no matching state schema, migrations, restore hooks or command-hash reconciliation exist. A generic JSON custom entry does not implement these transitions.',
 'Add a serde state representation and explicit tolerant migration decoder in ice-harness. Reuse the session append/branch APIs once their parity is established. Store only copies of process-authority observations; enforce current authority separately. Preserve JS safe-integer checks and exact JSON hash serialization, including property order. Cross-area host requirements: session_start/session_tree/session_shutdown, branch custom records, stale-context guards and ordered persistence.',
 'Resumption must not silently grant stale authority or discard approved-plan requirements.');
add(4,'Effective tool authority by mode, origin and declared access','P0',[180,300],
 ref(24,79)+'; '+ref(863,895)+'; '+ref(1626,1658)+'; '+ref(1813,1823)+'. Symbols IceCapabilityState, isExternalTool/effectiveTools; tool_call/user_bash hooks. Tests: '+tests(409,558)+'; '+tests(576,683)+'; '+tests(1156,1196)+'.',
 'The guard controls both the tool list shown to the model and actual tool-call admission. Plan/build, current trust and explicit process opt-ins determine access; names alone do not identify installed-package tools.',
 'Start with the exact PLAN_TOOLS or BUILD_TOOLS arrays below. Add non-external extension tools declaring access=read in either mode. Add non-external access=write extension tools only in trusted build. Undeclared inline tools remain inactive. External means exact name mcp, prefix mcp__, sourceInfo.origin=package, or exact cognee_search; trusted build with allow-external adds all currently registered external tools. This classification takes precedence over declared read access: package read tools still need external opt-in. Trusted build plus ice-allow-bash adds bash, bash_output, bash_kill, bash_watch, bash_input. The arrays may mention legacy tool names that are no longer registered; an allowlist name is not proof that a runtime tool exists.\n\nRemove read_plan when no saved plan; add it in plan mode once any plan exists. setActiveTools receives this array; there is no de-duplication here. At tool_call, recompute the effective set and block any absent name with "ICE <mode> mode blocks tool <quoted name>"; absent state acts fail-closed. Guard user Bash independently: unless effective Bash is true, return {result:{output:"ICE <mode> mode blocks user Bash",exitCode:1,cancelled:false,truncated:false}}.\n\nImportant source correction: built-in edit/write are present in BUILD_TOOLS even in an untrusted project. Trust gates Bash, external and declared extension writes, not those two built-ins. Also only edit/write/integrate_writer_patch/agent_patch apply participate in the approved-plan read gate and mutation accounting. Other extension write tools are not automatically routed through those checks. --allow-external has no hasUI condition in this guard; headless approval enforcement is delegated to the MCP adapter. Do not convert the warning about unrestricted access into an OS-sandbox claim.',
 quote(main,24,79)+'\nTool access metadata: access?: "read"|"write"; origin discriminator sourceInfo.origin === "package". Consumes tool_call and user_bash; may return block/reason or replacement user-Bash result. No additional settings, env vars, keybindings, RPC commands or persistence beyond SAFE-003.',
 ['SAFE-001','SAFE-003','SAFE-005','SAFE-013'],
 'Rust supports tool selection and generic blocking hooks: rust:crates/ice-agent/src/hooks.rs:73-84,99-130; rust:crates/ice-extensions/src/actions.rs:400-405,881-923. It lacks the ICE origin/access policy and mode-dependent enforcement. Tool write execution at rust:crates/ice-tools/src/tools/write.rs:84-138 proceeds from path resolution to mutation queue without an ICE guard check.',
 'Implement policy in ice-harness; expose immutable effective capabilities to child admission. Extend plugin tool metadata with access/origin only if equivalent fields are not already present after the extension audit. Enforce at dispatch as well as discovery. Security decision to record: whether the Rust target intentionally tightens built-in untrusted-write behavior; that is not faithful parity and must be approved/documented separately.',
 'Tool visibility without dispatch enforcement does not preserve parent authority.');
add(5,'Prospective-path and protected-file mutation checks','P0',[160,280],
 ref(322,397)+'; '+ref(1635,1656)+'. Exported resolveProspectivePath, pathIsWithin, validateMutationPath. Tests: '+tests(125,167)+'.',
 'Direct edit/write calls are constrained to the guarded tree and cannot target Git internals, environment files or credential files unless effective external access is enabled.',
 'Require a nonempty string path, then resolve it lexically against ctx.cwd. If lstat succeeds, use realpathSync on the target (so a dangling symlink fails). Otherwise climb parents while existsSync is false, collect each basename in front of a suffix list, realpath the first existing ancestor, and append the suffix. Resolution failure returns a block reason rather than throwing from the hook. Compare normalized resolved root and candidate; on Windows only the containment comparison lowercases both. Accept an empty relative path, or a relative path that is not .., does not begin ../ (platform separator), and is not absolute. Sibling prefix matches are not accepted.\n\nWithout effective external access, deny containment failure. Then inspect both lexical and canonical paths relative to root, split by platform separator: deny an exact .git segment; exact .env or any segment starting .env.; exact credentials.json or service-account.json. These checks apply to directory segments too. They are case-sensitive even on Windows, unlike containment normalization. Names such as my.git-parser.ts and environment.md are allowed. With effective external access, return success immediately after resolution and skip containment and every protected-name check.\n\nApply this only to edit/write. Writer integration and agent_patch apply have separate patch safeguards, not this path checker. Validation and later mutation are not one atomic filesystem operation; there is a symlink/time-of-check race. No file lock, directory descriptor or sandbox is created by this function.',
 '| Function | Input | Output |\n|---|---|---|\n| validateMutationPath | unknown path, cwd string, canonicalRoot string, allowExternal boolean=false | undefined on admission; human-readable reason otherwise |\n| resolveProspectivePath | path string | canonical/prospective absolute path; throws on resolution error |\n| pathIsWithin | root and candidate strings | boolean |\n\nErrors distinguish missing/nonstring path, resolution failure, outside root, protected .git data, protected environment file and protected credential file. No env/settings/file-format/CLI addition beyond SAFE-001.',
 ['SAFE-002','SAFE-004'],
 'rust:crates/ice-tools/src/path_utils.rs:28-92 performs normalization/read-path fallback, not protected-path admission. rust:crates/ice-tools/src/file_mutation_queue.rs:75-120 serializes by canonical/absolute key but is not a root or secret-file guard. rust:crates/ice-tools/src/tools/write.rs:84-138 has no equivalent checks.',
 'Use std::fs::symlink_metadata/canonicalize and Path components, but reproduce lexical+canonical name checks and prospective missing-leaf behavior. Place checks before both native edit/write execution. A race-resistant openat/capability-directory design would be a deliberate hardening difference; do not silently describe it as the current TS algorithm. Windows case-sensitive protected-name behavior is another explicit risk.',
 'This is the direct filesystem authority boundary for guarded mutations.');
add(6,'Manual plan/build transitions and pending-plan override','P1',[100,180],
 ref(942,981)+'; '+ref(1530,1583)+'. private setMode/approvePendingPlan; commands plan/build/ice-plan-review. Tests: '+tests(938,1044)+'.',
 'Users can toggle planning, enter guarded build manually, or reopen draft review without losing the saved plan.',
 '/plan toggles mode. From plan, if status is draft or pending and hasUI, ask "Exit plan mode?" with body "This enters guarded build mode without approving the current plan." and full Markdown content; false leaves everything unchanged. /build asks "Build without plan approval?" with the explicit-manual-override body under the same draft/pending+UI condition. Without UI those confirmation branches are skipped; these commands do not independently enforce a headless approval requirement. Neither manual transition changes draft/pending into approved.\n\nsetMode(plan) on an actual change captures current provider/model and thinking, resets reminder count, and retains the existing draft/approval. setMode(build), including an unchanged build request, resets readInBuild and reminders. Recompute current-process Bash observation; set active tools; append state; apply mode model; publish frozen capabilities; update ice-mode status and notify; issue sticky safety warnings if Bash/external effective; invoke onModeChange last.\n\n/ice-plan-review requires plan mode and nonempty saved Markdown. No plan emits a warning; already-approved emits info; otherwise set pending, reset reminders, persist, and call the review UI. A headless call leaves pending without selecting approval.',
 '| Command | Arguments | Effect |\n|---|---|---|\n| /plan | ignored | toggle plan/build with UI-only unfinished-plan confirmation |\n| /build | ignored | enter build, preserving unapproved draft and resetting read acknowledgement |\n| /ice-plan-review | ignored | turn draft/pending into pending and reopen explicit review |\n\nUI status key ice-mode; sticky notification IDs safety:bash and safety:external. No keybinding, setting, env or new RPC shape.',
 ['SAFE-003','SAFE-004','SAFE-007','SAFE-012','SAFE-025'],
 'Native command registration and active-tool actions exist (rust:crates/ice-extensions/src/actions.rs:400-405,881-923), but no ICE mode-transition commands or stored plan state. Rendering plan_mode_* at rust:crates/ice-cli/src/transcript_view.rs:348,400,524 does not supply these transitions.',
 'Route native CLI/slash commands to one guard state service in ice-harness. Serialize transition/persist/capability publication ordering. A UI-only confirmation in TS is not a universal trust gate; record any stricter headless Rust behavior as different-by-design.',
 'Users need reproducible mode changes without silently approving unfinished plans.');
add(7,'Planning/execution model selection and thinking restoration','P1',[100,200],
 ref(417,438)+'; '+ref(908,965)+'; '+ref(1225,1239)+'; '+ref(1258,1274)+'. private modelReference/parseModelFlag/resolveModelReference/applyModeModel/selectExecutionModel. Tests: '+tests(1076,1098)+'.',
 'Planning may use one model and approved execution another, while restoring the pre-planning thinking level.',
 'Canonical reference is provider + "/" + id. A configured reference is trimmed; resolve against ctx.scopedModels when nonempty, otherwise modelRegistry.getAvailable(). Case-insensitively match a unique canonical reference first, then a unique bare id; zero or multiple matches fail resolution with warning. On plan entry use only ice-plan-model if configured. On build use saved plan.executionModel, then ice-build-model, then prePlanModel. A failed lookup or setModel(false) notifies and leaves the current model; it does not abort mode transition. If already on target, still restore saved thinking in build. After successful build switch restore saved thinking too.\n\nApproval may show a second selector only when at least two unique canonical models occur in scopedModels. Deduplicate by canonical reference retaining map insertion order. Labels append (configured) on exact match to the configured string, else (current) on exact current reference; configuration precedence wins. Choice cancellation gives undefined, retaining fallback behavior; strip one trailing configured/current suffix from a selection. The selector does not use all available models when the scope is empty. Store the chosen executionModel with approval; fresh draft replacement clears it. Capture prePlanModel/prePlanThinkingLevel only on an actual transition into plan or initial state creation.',
 '| Interface | Type/default |\n|---|---|\n| --ice-plan-model | optional trimmed string |\n| --ice-build-model | optional trimmed string |\n| plan.prePlanModel / executionModel | optional provider/model string |\n| plan.prePlanThinkingLevel | off,minimal,low,medium,high,xhigh,max,ultra |\n| approval selector | title "Continue approved plan with" |\n\nConsumes scopedModels, modelRegistry, setModel and setThinkingLevel. No new provider, env, keybinding or RPC.',
 ['SAFE-003','SAFE-006','SAFE-012'],
 'Rust has model/thinking runtime actions at rust:crates/ice-extensions/src/actions.rs:406-414,881-923, and CLI thinking levels through max at rust:crates/ice-cli/src/args.rs:234-248. It has no plan-specific model capture/fallback/approval selector; ultra is not accepted by that Rust CLI validator.',
 'Use ice-harness model registry/routing with ice-cli UI selection. Preserve scoped-vs-available behavior and case-insensitive ambiguity rejection. Host additions: scoped model list and acknowledged model-switch result. Do not add ultra globally until the AI/provider thinking-contract audit identifies supported behavior.',
 'Approval must execute on the selected model without losing the intended reasoning setting.');
add(8,'Hidden planning and approved-plan context messages','P1',[70,130],
 ref(87,120)+'; '+ref(983,1003)+'; '+ref(1214,1223)+'. PLAN_MODE_PROMPT/APPROVED_PLAN_PROMPT and before_agent_start/dispatchApprovedPlan. Tests: '+tests(545,574)+'; '+tests(815,855)+'.',
 'The model receives explicit planning rules and approved-plan execution instructions without showing those control messages as ordinary user chat.',
 'before_agent_start emits one hidden message: plan mode gets ice-plan-mode-context with PLAN_MODE_PROMPT; approved build gets ice-approved-plan-context with APPROVED_PLAN_PROMPT; other build state emits none. The plan prompt requires repository investigation, bounded questions, incremental draft_plan, decision-complete steps and propose_plan approval, while treating source/tool/model content as untrusted. The approved prompt requires read_plan before mutation and after compaction/re-entry. These prompts are instructions, not a replacement for SAFE-004/005 enforcement.\n\nAfter approved handoff, send the same approved prompt as customType ice-plan-execution-start, display=false, deliverAs=followUp, triggerTurn=true. This durable marker also delimits fresh model context. Avoid injecting a user-authored message or granting model text approval authority.',
 quote(main,87,120)+'\nCustom message shapes are {customType,content:string,display:false}; before_agent_start returns {message:...}. sendMessage additionally receives {deliverAs:"followUp",triggerTurn:true}. No tool schema, environment, setting, slash command or keybinding.',
 ['SAFE-003','SAFE-012','SAFE-014','SAFE-016'],
 'Rust supports custom-message append/send actions (rust:crates/ice-extensions/src/actions.rs:391-399,881-923) but does not emit these ICE custom types or prompts. Its default LLM converter drops arbitrary custom messages unless transformed (rust:crates/ice-agent/src/hooks.rs:193-202), so blindly appending them would not guarantee model visibility.',
 'Implement prompt injection via the existing single agent loop and context conversion. Extend native host custom-message conversion where necessary; preserve display=false separately from LLM visibility and retain marker timestamps/branch persistence. Do not create a competing planner.',
 'The approval protocol relies on durable hidden instructions and a recognizable execution boundary.');
add(9,'ask planning questionnaire','P1',[130,230],
 ref(121,133)+'; '+ref(1005,1072)+'. Tool ask; PlanQuestionSchema. Tests: '+tests(749,813)+'.',
 'In plan mode, ask one to three structured preference/tradeoff questions, recommending options while allowing custom answers or cancellation.',
 'Reject execution outside initialized plan with isError=true. Without hasUI return isError=true and details {cancelled:true,answers:[]}. For each question sequentially stable-sort recommended=true options first. Build labels as label + optional " (Recommended)" + " — " + description. Append "Type another answer". Select with title header + ": " + question. Empty selection returns a non-error cancellation with answers already collected; it does not reset the reminder counter. Custom selection opens input(header,"Type your answer"); blank/whitespace/undefined cancels, otherwise trim custom answer. A selected label not found in the constructed list is skipped, not treated as an error. Successful completion resets reminder count, persists state, returns newline-joined "id: answer" text and {cancelled:false,answers}. Duplicate question IDs/labels are not separately rejected by this tool. Signal/onUpdate parameters are unused; UI cancellation is the mechanism here.',
 quote(main,121,133)+'\nOuter parameters: Type.Object({ questions: Type.Array(PlanQuestionSchema, { minItems: 1, maxItems: 3 }) }). All string schema maxima are TypeBox character limits; unlike draft_plan, this tool adds no byte-limit/NUL validation. Result is {content:[{type:"text",text}],details:{cancelled:boolean,answers:Array<{id:string,answer:string}>},isError?:boolean}. No settings/env/slash/keybindings/RPC/file writes apart from guard-state append.',
 ['SAFE-003','SAFE-004','SAFE-016'],
 'Rust has a general interactive dialog request/poll/cancel mailbox, including headless rejection and tool-call cancellation (rust:crates/ice-extensions/src/actions.rs:99-360). It does not register this ask tool, schema, multi-question recommendation ordering or persisted reminder reset.',
 'Register a native tool in ice-harness or a mandatory guard plugin; reuse ice-cli dialog UI. The plugin host must support select/input results and tool lifetime. Preserve partial answers on cancellation, and distinguish error (unavailable UI) from user cancellation.',
 'Structured planning decisions must be available before explicit approval.');
add(10,'draft_plan bounded session-native Markdown drafts','P1',[100,180],
 ref(80,82)+'; '+ref(399,405)+'; '+ref(441,454)+'; '+ref(1074,1120)+'. Tool draft_plan; private validatePlanText/planHash. Tests: '+tests(685,747)+'.',
 'The model creates or replaces the current plan in durable session state without writing a repository Markdown file.',
 'Require initialized plan mode. Validate nonempty trimmed title, raw title UTF-8 bytes <=512, nonempty trimmed Markdown with raw UTF-8 bytes <=65536, and no NUL in either. Store trimmed title but original Markdown, including surrounding whitespace. Hash JSON.stringify({title,markdown}) using SHA-256 hex, with that property order and UTF-8 encoding. Replace the entire plan with status draft, content/hash, readInBuild=false, reminder count 0, preserving only prePlanModel and prePlanThinkingLevel from the old plan. This deliberately clears approval policy/time/cutoff/executionModel. Persist before applyTools; this makes read_plan available. Return "Plan draft saved: <title>" and details {status:"draft",title}. Caught validation errors return their message, undefined details and isError=true.',
 quote(main,1079,1082)+'\nRuntime byte bounds supplement TypeBox minLength/maxLength, so multibyte text may pass schema length and fail runtime bytes. No arbitrary path parameter. Storage is SAFE-003 custom state only, never a model-selected file. No env/settings/slash/keybindings/RPC.',
 ['SAFE-003','SAFE-004','SAFE-013'],
 'Rust append_entry support exists at rust:crates/ice-extensions/src/actions.rs:393-395,881-923, but no bounded session-native plan schema, replacement rules or content hash tool exists. Generic write is not an equivalent because it writes the working tree.',
 'Use serde_json deterministic field ordering matching the two TS properties plus sha2. Implement text-byte validation before persistence; do not rely on Rust JSON Schema string lengths alone. Place state ownership in ice-harness rather than independent plugin storage.',
 'Drafts are the durable approval object and cannot be substituted by transient model prose.');
add(11,'propose_plan approval submission and retry behavior','P1',[100,180],
 ref(1122,1185)+'. Tool propose_plan. Tests: '+tests(717,747)+'; '+tests(804,855)+'; '+tests(938,981)+'.',
 'Only a saved draft can be submitted for explicit review. Headless execution stores a pending proposal and does not approve it automatically.',
 'Require initialized plan mode. Require status exactly draft, saved title equal to params.title.trim(), and truthy stored Markdown/hash. Missing/mismatched/non-draft state throws "Draft plan not found. Call draft_plan before propose_plan." even if a pending draft with the same title exists. Snapshot title/content/hash locally, set pending/readInBuild=false/reminders0, persist and refresh tools. With UI await SAFE-012, then return approved/cancelled/pending wording according to current state plus details {status,title}. The none/cancelled branch exists defensively but the current review selector does not itself clear the plan. Without UI return "Plan proposal pending approval: <title>" and pending details. Exceptions from validation/review are returned as isError=true; already-persisted pending state is not rolled back. Reopening a pending proposal uses /ice-plan-review, not another propose_plan call unless draft_plan first creates a new draft.',
 quote(main,1127,1127)+'\nTool result: content text and details {status: none|draft|pending|approved,title:string}, or undefined details + isError=true on error. Consumes explicit UI decision; no model output is approval. No env/settings/keybinding/RPC or repository file.',
 ['SAFE-010','SAFE-012','SAFE-006'],
 'No registered propose_plan contract in Rust. Generic native tool and UI APIs at rust:crates/ice-extensions/src/actions.rs:99-360,381-499 can support it but do not persist pending state or enforce draft identity.',
 'Implement as one guard-service transaction before opening UI. Preserve the pending state on review failure and prevent repeated calls from treating an already-pending object as a new draft. Host needs content-bearing selection dialogs, not a yes/no model tool.',
 'Proposal identity and durable pending status are prerequisites for trustworthy approval.');
add(12,'Explicit review, approval identity and settled-turn handoff','P0',[180,300],
 ref(83,86)+'; '+ref(1241,1301)+'; '+ref(1744,1749)+'. private approvePendingPlan/beginApprovedPlanHandoff. Tests: '+tests(815,890)+'; '+tests(938,981)+'.',
 'The user reviews the full plan and chooses fresh, compacted or retained execution context. Build begins at a safe turn boundary and always requires reading the approved plan.',
 'Only initialized plan+pending+hasUI with nonempty Markdown opens selector "Plan mode - next step" with the exact four options below and {content:planMarkdown}. Refine or dismiss merely notifies "ICE plan remains pending approval."; it does not reopen an editor, send a model prompt, cancel the draft or change mode. For approval map execute→fresh, compact→compact, keep→keep. Capture approvedAt=Date.now() before the optional execution-model selector. Store approved status, readInBuild=false, reminders0, approvalMode, approvedAt, contextCutoffAt=approvedAt only for fresh, and chosen executionModel. Persist before dispatch.\n\nIf ctx.isIdle(), begin handoff immediately; otherwise call stopAfterTurn(), not abort(), and notify that build starts after this tool turn. agent_settled begins handoff only if still plan+approved. Handoff calls setMode(build) first, then SAFE-015 for compact or immediate hidden execution-start follow-up otherwise. The method has no independent hash/session recheck after awaiting UI; porting a stronger reentrancy check is a hardening change, not an observed guarantee. Automatic headless print/json plan settlement returns before handoff; RPC is not excluded by that specific early-return condition.',
 '| Exact review label | Saved policy |\n|---|---|\n| Approve and execute | fresh |\n| Approve and compact context | compact |\n| Approve and keep context | keep |\n| Refine plan | no state transition; pending remains |\n\nConsumes agent_settled, hasUI, isIdle, stopAfterTurn, select(content), compact(callbacks); emits hidden follow-up in SAFE-008. No approval token is accepted from the model. No setting/env/keybinding/new RPC schema.',
 ['SAFE-003','SAFE-006','SAFE-007','SAFE-008','SAFE-013','SAFE-014','SAFE-015'],
 'Generic UI and compact actions exist at rust:crates/ice-extensions/src/actions.rs:99-360,415-431,881-923. They do not implement this approved-plan transition or stop-after-current-tool-turn sequencing. Rust transcript plan rendering is presentation only.',
 'Keep approval and handoff in the single existing ice-harness loop. Required host additions: stop-after-turn distinct from cancellation, agent_settled delivery after all tool results, content-bearing plan selector and async compaction completion/error callbacks. Preserve explicit user approval rather than infer it from a plan panel.',
 'This is the authority transition from model-authored draft to executable scope.');
add(13,'read_plan acknowledgement and post-compaction mutation gate','P0',[80,150],
 ref(892,894)+'; '+ref(1186,1212)+'; '+ref(1635,1655)+'; '+ref(1807,1812)+'. Tool read_plan; session_compact hook. Tests: '+tests(685,715)+'; '+tests(983,1018)+'; '+tests(1122,1141)+'; '+tests(1220,1259)+'.',
 'An approved plan must be reread before direct edits, writes and explicit patch application after approval, build re-entry or compaction.',
 'Hide read_plan entirely while plan.status=none. With any saved plan, return the exact stored Markdown and details status/title/contentHash. No plan or missing title/Markdown returns isError=true and "No plan has been proposed.". A successful read in approved build, with readInBuild=false, sets true and persists before returning. Reads in plan/draft/pending do not acknowledge build authority.\n\nThe tool_call gate covers edit, write, integrate_writer_patch, and agent_patch only when input.action===apply. If approved build and unread, block with "Read approved plan with read_plan before mutation" before path checking or authorized-ID recording. session_compact clears and persists readInBuild only when approved and currently true. setMode(build) resets it even when build was already active; restore does not automatically reset it. Bash and arbitrary declared extension writes are not covered by this acknowledgement check in current source.',
 'Parameters: Type.Object({}). Result: {content:[{type:"text",text:markdown}],details:{status,title,contentHash}}. Error has undefined details and isError=true. State: plan.readInBuild:boolean. Consumes session_compact; no CLI/env/settings/keybinding/RPC addition.',
 ['SAFE-003','SAFE-004','SAFE-006','SAFE-012'],
 'Rust write execution at rust:crates/ice-tools/src/tools/write.rs:84-138 does not require a plan receipt. Generic before-tool hooks exist (rust:crates/ice-agent/src/hooks.rs:73-84), but no stored approved-plan acknowledgement or compaction reset is wired to them.',
 'Place the acknowledgement in the guard state and check before acquiring write/patch authority. Extend native compaction completion events to reset it. Do not implement this solely as a prompt or per-tool local flag. Decide explicitly whether shell/other write paths should gain a stricter gate than TS.',
 'A durable approved plan alone does not ensure the execution context has read it.');
add(14,'Fresh approved-plan context projection and orphan-result pruning','P1',[80,150],
 ref(1773,1806)+'; '+src('packages/coding-agent/src/core/legacy-compat/identity.ts',1,3)+'. context hook. Tests: '+tests(892,936)+'.',
 'Fresh execution excludes prior planning context while retaining the durable session history and avoiding orphan tool results in the next model request.',
 'Run only in build with approved plan, policy fresh and defined contextCutoffAt. Scan messages backward for the latest role=custom and exact customType ice-plan-execution-start. If found, retain that marker and everything after it. Otherwise retain messages with timestamp >= cutoff. Collect every toolCall.id from assistant content in the retained subset, then remove toolResult messages whose toolCallId is not in that set. Return {messages:filtered}; do not delete session entries or alter the plan. The ID set is not position-sensitive: a retained result is accepted if its call occurs anywhere in the retained subset. Non-tool messages with missing timestamps fail the timestamp fallback comparison but can remain when marker slicing is used. The latest marker wins across repeated handoffs.',
 'Consumes context event with messages containing role, timestamp, customType, assistant content/toolCall.id or toolResult.toolCallId. Returns replacement messages only. Uses stored approvalMode/contextCutoffAt and the exact hidden marker. No external binary, file format, setting, env, tool, CLI or keybinding.',
 ['SAFE-003','SAFE-008','SAFE-012'],
 'Rust supports transform_context and convert_to_llm callbacks (rust:crates/ice-agent/src/hooks.rs:29-34,99-130). It lacks this marker/cutoff projection and associated orphan-result rule; generic transform capability is not behavioral parity.',
 'Implement one context projection in ice-harness before provider conversion, preserving complete on-disk history. Reuse message IDs and custom-message timestamps; do not simulate fresh context by truncating the JSONL file. Explicitly preserve tool call/result consistency.',
 'Fresh approval must not leak superseded planning context or send unmatched tool results.');
add(15,'Compacted and retained approval-context handoffs','P1',[70,130],
 ref(115,118)+'; '+ref(1284,1301)+'. beginApprovedPlanHandoff/PLAN_COMPACTION_PROMPT. Tests: '+tests(857,890)+'.',
 'Approval can compact planning context before starting execution, or keep it intact, without losing the durable approved plan.',
 'After mode becomes build, compact policy invokes ctx.compact with the exact custom instructions below. Both onComplete and onError enqueue the hidden execution-start follow-up. On error first warn "Plan compaction failed; continuing with existing context: <message>". Failure does not revoke approval or stop execution, but read_plan remains required. Keep policy dispatches immediately without compaction and without fresh-context filtering. Fresh also dispatches immediately but is filtered by SAFE-014. The command uses callback completion; it does not await a Promise from compact. Handoff notification states that read_plan is required.',
 quote(main,115,118)+'\nCompact request: {customInstructions:string,onComplete:dispatchApprovedPlan,onError:(error)=>notifyAndDispatch}. Hidden follow-up shape is SAFE-008. No new settings/env/CLI/slash/keybinding/tool parameters.',
 ['SAFE-006','SAFE-008','SAFE-012','SAFE-013','SAFE-014'],
 'Rust exposes a generic compact(args) runtime action (rust:crates/ice-extensions/src/actions.rs:415-416,881-923) and an after_tool_results loop hook (rust:crates/ice-agent/src/hooks.rs:59-64). These contradict a blanket claim that compaction is absent, but neither supplies this approval-specific callback/fallback policy.',
 'Use existing ice-harness compaction rather than a second summarizer. Bridge completion and failure back to ordered follow-up delivery. Ensure no double dispatch if callbacks race or session ownership expires; current TS does not explicitly guard callback reentrancy here.',
 'Context-policy selection must have defined execution behavior when compaction fails.');
add(16,'Bounded prose-only planning continuations and abort suppression','P1',[90,160],
 ref(82,82)+'; '+ref(119,120)+'; '+ref(1626,1634)+'; '+ref(1726,1772)+'. agent_start/agent_end/turn_end/agent_settled hooks. Tests: '+tests(1030,1074)+'.',
 'An interactive planning run that ends with prose instead of a useful tool action can be continued automatically, at most three times, without restarting a deliberately aborted run.',
 'At agent_start clear last-turn tool/decision flags, scheduled flag and aborted flag. At turn_end in plan for an assistant message, record whether there is any toolCall and whether any is ask/propose_plan. At admitted ask/propose_plan tool_call reset reminder count and persist; successful ask and draft_plan also reset it. At agent_end, if the final message is assistant with stopReason=aborted, mark the run aborted.\n\nAt agent_settled, headless print/json plan returns immediately. Approved plan handoff takes precedence. Otherwise remind only for plan, status !=pending, no tool calls, no decision, no continuation already scheduled in this run, no deliberate abort and persisted counter <3. Increment/persist before sending hidden ice-plan-decision-reminder with PLAN_DECISION_REMINDER, followUp, triggerTurn=true; return without verifying that settlement. Any tool call, including ordinary read, suppresses this prose-only branch; it is not merely an ask/propose absence check. If no reminder/handoff applies, attempt ordinary verification. RPC is not covered by the print/json early return, so a no-UI RPC context can satisfy reminder conditions.',
 'Limit MAX_PLAN_DECISION_REMINDERS=3. Hidden type ice-plan-decision-reminder, display=false; content exactly the PLAN_DECISION_REMINDER declaration in SAFE-008. Persisted plan.decisionReminderCount; transient four booleans per run. No new setting, env, CLI, keybinding or model tool.',
 ['SAFE-003','SAFE-008','SAFE-009','SAFE-010','SAFE-012','SAFE-021'],
 'Rust steering/follow-up hooks exist at rust:crates/ice-agent/src/hooks.rs:66-69,99-130. It has no ICE reminder counter, turn-action classification or Escape/abort suppression for planning continuations.',
 'Integrate with existing settlement and follow-up queues in ice-harness; do not start a parallel planner. Distinguish user abort from ordinary completion and persist the cap before scheduling. Match print/json/RPC distinctions rather than using one blanket headless branch.',
 'Unbounded or abort-insensitive continuation would waste requests and violate user interruption.');
add(17,'Authorized native mutation generations','P0',[90,170],
 ref(832,832)+'; '+ref(1635,1661)+'; '+ref(1715,1725)+'; '+ref(1841,1841)+'; '+ref(1889,1889)+'. authorizedMutations set, tool_call/tool_result. Tests: '+tests(1198,1218)+'; '+tests(1330,1348)+'.',
 'Verification freshness advances only after a matching, admitted native mutation completes successfully, not from arbitrary tool-result text.',
 'After active-tool admission, approved-plan read gate and path check, add toolCallId to an in-memory Set for edit/write/legacy patch integration/agent_patch apply. On tool_result, delete that ID first; if it was absent, state is absent, or event.isError, ignore. For edit/write increment mutationGeneration once. When a verifier is configured replace verifier with pending, new generation and current command hash; otherwise keep the previous verifier state. Persist full state. Duplicate results cannot increment because the first deletes the ID. Failed calls consume authorization without increment; unknown successful results do nothing. Restore and shutdown clear pending authorizations.\n\nThe set has no mutex because JS callbacks run through event dispatch, but it persists across awaited executions. It is not a filesystem watcher: Bash, external edits, arbitrary extension writes and changes outside these observed tool paths do not increment the counter. A verification generation is not evidence that every file is unchanged. Patch-specific accounting is SAFE-018.',
 'Consumes tool_call {toolCallId,toolName,input} and tool_result {toolCallId,toolName,isError,details?}. Writes mutationGeneration and optional verifier {status:"pending",generation,commandHash}. No standalone telemetry event or watcher is emitted here. No new CLI/env/setting/keybinding.',
 ['SAFE-003','SAFE-004','SAFE-005','SAFE-013','SAFE-019'],
 'Rust has before/after-tool callbacks (rust:crates/ice-agent/src/hooks.rs:73-84) and per-path mutation serialization (rust:crates/ice-tools/src/file_mutation_queue.rs:99-120), but neither keeps the ICE authorization-ID set or generation evidence. The Rust SDK ToolResult view carries IDs/name/result JSON/is_error (rust:crates/ice-plugin-sdk/src/events.rs:14-19,95-113), providing raw inputs for an implementation.',
 'Keep generation/accounting in ice-harness, shared with verifier and child patch integration. Require matching tool identity as a possible hardening improvement; current TS consumes by ID and then branches on result toolName. Do not treat successful shell execution as accounted mutation without a separately specified policy.',
 'Verification receipts must be tied to observed mutations and must not be forgeable by unmatched results.');
add(18,'Subagent patch verification import and conflict accounting','P0',[90,180],
 ref(1661,1714)+'. tool_result patch branches. Tests: '+tests(1220,1328)+'.',
 'A verified applied child patch advances both mutation and checked generations without rerunning the same verifier; unverified application and rollback conflicts remain distinguishable.',
 'Require a consumed authorized ID and isError=false as in SAFE-017. For integrate_writer_patch with details.status=integrated, or agent_patch with details.status=applied, require an object verification with status passed. Increment generation and set checkedGeneration to it; copy the verification object and override its generation with the new parent generation; persist. This branch does not independently compare the child commandHash to the current parent argv hash.\n\nFor agent_patch with rollback_conflict, increment mutationGeneration and set verifier {status:"pending",generation:new}; no commandHash is added in that branch and checkedGeneration stays unchanged. For agent_patch applied with unverified===true, increment generation; if parent verifier configured mark pending with its hash, otherwise retain prior verifier. Other patch statuses make no counter change, including applied without either passed verification or unverified=true. Any isError result is rejected before patch branching, including failed legacy integration/conflict statuses. Ordinary settlement skips a just-imported verified generation because checked==mutation.',
 'Expected details variants: {status:"integrated"|"applied",verification:{status:"passed",...IceVerifierState}}; {status:"rollback_conflict"}; {status:"applied",unverified:true}. Admission for agent_patch requires input.action==="apply". No new tool is registered by this guard; patch schema/transaction belongs to subagents.md.',
 ['SAFE-003','SAFE-013','SAFE-017','SAFE-021'],
 'Rust generic child/runtime actions exist at rust:crates/ice-extensions/src/actions.rs:1126-1163, but no ICE patch-to-guard verification receipt accounting exists. Native write serialization is not equivalent to applying a child worktree transaction with imported verifier evidence.',
 'Join the parent guard service to the Rust child-patch transaction result, not to human-readable result text. Specify a typed receipt with status/hash/generation. Decide explicitly whether to add current-command-hash validation; current TS trusts the passed receipt from its own patch implementation.',
 'Without this bridge, child writes can either evade verification or cause redundant verifier execution.');
add(19,'Trusted verifier argv validation and command identity','P0',[70,130],
 ref(134,144)+'; '+ref(293,320)+'; '+ref(399,401)+'; '+ref(1829,1831)+'. Exported parseVerifierArgv/getConfiguredIceVerifierArgv. Tests: '+tests(114,122)+'; '+src(htest,179,206)+'.',
 'A verifier is a bounded, explicit argument vector from the current process configuration, never a model-supplied shell string.',
 'undefined or boolean false disables verification; any other non-string value errors. Bound the raw JSON text to 16384 UTF-8 bytes before parsing. JSON parse failure becomes "--ice-verify must be valid JSON" with cause. Require an array of 1..64 elements, each a string with length >0, no NUL and <=4096 UTF-8 bytes. Whitespace-only arguments are accepted; there is no executable allowlist or shell metacharacter filtering because shell=false. This validates JSON text and per-argument bounds, not a separately bounded decoded total.\n\nIdentity is lowercase SHA-256 hex over UTF-8 JSON.stringify(argv), with compact JSON serialization. Restore reads the flag again and stores a module-level clone for other trusted components. getConfiguredIceVerifierArgv returns a fresh clone or undefined, preventing callers from mutating the stored vector. Neither argv nor mutable command selection is exposed through the Goals verify request.',
 '| Constant/API | Exact contract |\n|---|---|\n| MAX_VERIFY_TOTAL_BYTES | 16384 raw JSON bytes |\n| MAX_VERIFY_ARGS | 64 |\n| MAX_VERIFY_ARG_BYTES | 4096 |\n| --ice-verify | string JSON array; absent/false disables |\n| getConfiguredIceVerifierArgv() | string[] copy or undefined |\n| commandHash | SHA-256 of compact JSON argv |\n\nNo environment variable, setting key, model tool parameter or arbitrary Goals argv field.',
 ['SAFE-001'],
 'rust:crates/ice-cli/src/args.rs:107-230,271-545 has no verifier argv flag/parser. Existing shell/tool process execution is not equivalent to a current-process trusted verifier identity.',
 'Parse in ice-cli using serde_json, validate UTF-8 byte lengths and NUL explicitly, hash with sha2. Keep argv in an immutable Arc-backed configuration or copied vector and expose only the hash to untrusted/model-facing contexts. Executable resolution is ordinary host PATH unless separately configured.',
 'The verification engine must not become an arbitrary model-controlled command-execution API.');
add(20,'Bounded verifier subprocess, timeout and cancellation','P0',[220,380],
 ref(456,630)+'; '+src('packages/coding-agent/src/utils/shell.ts',180,195)+'; '+src('packages/coding-agent/src/utils/shell.ts',243,267)+'. Exported runVerifier; private execVerifier/retainOutput/signalProcessTree. Tests: '+tests(1498,1576)+'.',
 'Run the configured verifier without a shell, cap captured output, terminate the process tree on timeout/cancellation and return structured nonpassing evidence for failures.',
 'Defaults: timeout120000ms, combined retained output65536bytes, termination grace5000ms. Spawn argv[0] with argv.slice(1), cwd=guarded root, shell=false, stdin ignored, stdout/stderr pipes, hidden Windows window, detached process group on non-Windows. Track child PID in the shared detached-child registry. Capture stdout/stderr buffers with a single remaining-byte budget in event arrival order while continuing to count/discard excess bytes. Native capture decodes each stream to UTF-8 on close. retainOutput then prioritizes stdout within the same total cap and gives remaining bytes to stderr; this also bounds injected verifierExec results. Byte slicing may split UTF-8 and lossy decoding may insert replacement characters; do not assert exact post-decoding byte equality for arbitrary Unicode.\n\nLink a private AbortController to request signal and a timer. Initial request abort marks cancelled but runVerifier still invokes the executor with an already-aborted signal; Goals prevents starting pre-aborted requests separately. Timer marks timedOut before aborting. On termination send SIGTERM to -pid, fallback pid on Unix; on Windows launch taskkill /T /PID without /F. Arm SIGKILL/tree force-kill once after grace. On child error, cleanup and reject; on close, clear force timer, untrack PID, remove abort listener, return code or1 if null plus output/killed/truncated. This implementation clears escalation on close; do not promise containment of descendants that detach or close all inherited pipes.\n\nrunVerifier computes status in priority timeout > cancellation > code0 passed > failed. On executor throw use timeout/cancel/spawn-error priority. Return commandHash, durationMs and, for normal completion, exitCode/output/truncated. failureMessage is exact timeout/cancel/exit description or thrown error text. Clean timer/listener in finally. The declared optional signal field is never populated; ExecResult.killed alone does not decide final status. An injected exec receives timeout and signal but owns its own output/process behavior.',
 quote(main,184,216)+'\nExported constants: VERIFIER_TIMEOUT_MS=120000, VERIFIER_OUTPUT_LIMIT_BYTES=65536, VERIFIER_TERMINATION_GRACE_MS=5000. OS helpers: taskkill on Windows; Unix process-group signaling. Native spawn inherits process environment by default; it does not call getShellEnv or a shell. No new env/setting/model tool/keybinding.',
 ['SAFE-002','SAFE-019'],
 'Rust generic tool execution/path infrastructure exists, but no configured-verifier receipt runner is connected to guard generations. Native extension runtime has cancellation-aware child actions (rust:crates/ice-extensions/src/actions.rs:1126-1163); that is not this bounded verifier. No signal receipt should be claimed present merely because Rust process APIs expose ExitStatus.',
 'Implement in ice-harness with tokio::process, CancellationToken, bounded byte buffers and platform process-group/job cleanup. Reuse existing process lifecycle utilities only after their semantics are audited. Rust crates already used by the workspace should be preferred; sha2/serde_json cover identity and serialization. Hardening candidates: directory/process capabilities, descendant cleanup after pipe closure and UTF-8-safe output caps.',
 'Verification must not hang the harness, leak unbounded output or falsely pass after cancellation.');
add(21,'Automatic/manual verification, durable receipts and lifecycle cleanup','P0',[190,330],
 ref(768,787)+'; '+ref(1348,1443)+'; '+ref(1584,1589)+'; '+ref(1744,1772)+'; '+ref(1882,1894)+'. private verify, /ice-verify, settlement/shutdown hooks. Tests: '+tests(1330,1450)+'.',
 'Run verification once for a newly observed mutation generation, allow an explicit rerun, persist running/final evidence, and make failed headless verification fail the process.',
 'verify returns undefined if no state or another run is active. With no configured argv, manual force only warns; automatic silently returns. Automatic runs only when mutationGeneration>checkedGeneration; force bypasses that comparison. This function itself does not require build or read_plan: Goals adds those gates, while /ice-verify can force a trusted-plan verifier. Untrusted verification never spawns: advance checkedGeneration to current, store blocked-untrusted/generation/hash/failureMessage, persist, report error, set process.exitCode=1 for print/json/rpc.\n\nBefore awaiting, set verifierRunning=true, persist running/generation/hash, link context and optional request aborts, capture UI if available and determine headless mode. Run at guardRoot. For ordinary verification, completion does not revalidate session epoch/root/mode/trust/current generation; it writes checkedGeneration=captured generation into then-current state. For Goals requests only, isCurrentGoalVerification can suppress receipt persistence (SAFE-024). Any passed result observed after context/request signal abortion is converted to cancelled. Persist receipt, update UI status ice-verify and notify or write headless stderr, and set nonzero headless exitCode on nonpass. Passing does not reset an earlier process exitCode=1.\n\nTrack active controller/completion/listeners; finally remove listeners, clear activeVerifier only if completion identity matches, and release verifierRunning. session_shutdown first invalidates Goals/session identities and authorization IDs, then aborts and awaits the active verifier, swallowing completion rejection. The regression requires old ctx.ui/mode getters not be accessed after asynchronous completion; capture them beforehand. Ordinary receipt persistence after stale-context completion is explicitly tested, so do not incorrectly describe it as full stale-generation rejection.',
 'Slash /ice-verify ignores arguments and calls verify(force=true). Status key ice-verify holds passed or failure status. Headless modes: print/json/rpc. Failure reports: exit-code failure, timed out, could not start, cancelled, blocked-untrusted. State running/final schemas are SAFE-003/020. No new settings/env/keybindings/tool parameters.',
 ['SAFE-003','SAFE-017','SAFE-018','SAFE-019','SAFE-020'],
 'Rust generic callbacks and custom append APIs (rust:crates/ice-agent/src/hooks.rs:99-130; rust:crates/ice-extensions/src/actions.rs:393-499) do not schedule verification by generation, persist ICE receipts or set corresponding headless exit status.',
 'One verifier service in ice-harness must be shared by settlement, manual command and Goals. Keep a singleflight token and capture immutable session identity before await. Preserving TS ordinary stale-receipt behavior versus strengthening it is an explicit open design question; do not silently claim the Goals stale guarantees apply to every caller.',
 'Automatic settlement evidence and process success must reflect observed verifier outcomes.');
add(22,'Versioned Goals host registry and lifecycle ownership','P1',[70,130],
 src(host,1,66)+'; '+ref(1523,1528)+'; '+ref(1882,1894)+'; '+src('packages/coding-agent/docs/ice-goals-host.md',1,45)+'. Exported ICE_GOALS_HOST_KEY, registerIceGoalsHost/getIceGoalsHost and host interfaces. Tests: '+src(htest,179,206)+'; '+src(htest,299,330)+'.',
 'Trusted goal extensions can discover the current parent guard controller without creating another planner, provider client or verifier.',
 'Register on the shared extension event-bus object at Symbol.for("ice.goals.host.v1") using Object.defineProperty(value=controller,configurable=true). Omitted descriptor flags mean nonenumerable and nonwritable. The disposer deletes only if the current property is still the identical controller, so an old disposer cannot remove a replacement. Discovery accepts only a nonempty controller with version exactly1 and callable snapshot/verify; otherwise return undefined. It does not clone or freeze the controller.\n\nThe guard creates exactly {version:1,snapshot,verify} and registers it at extension initialization. Calls fail until restore establishes an active session. Shutdown marks inactive, increments epoch, clears session identity, marks an active Goals run inactive, unregisters and then aborts/awaits the verifier. A retained controller reference therefore cannot operate after unregister. The optional external pi-goal-x consumer is not loaded by default; declaration of Workgraph intent does not imply a goal scheduler exists in core.',
 quote(host,3,34)+'\nRegistry key is a global symbol, not an environment variable or settings key. No arbitrary argv, permission mutation, mode change or model routing API. No model-facing Goals tool is implemented by this host file; GOAL_TOOLS in SAFE-004 is an allowlist only.',
 ['SAFE-003','SAFE-023','SAFE-024'],
 'rust:crates/ice-extensions/src/actions.rs:381-499 and dispatcher881-923 expose no versioned Goals controller. Runtime stale-handle rejection and reload ownership exist at 527-614,759-777,984-1019, but are generic lifetime primitives, not this registry/contract.',
 'Expose versioned native host actions or an extension-service registry through ice-plugin-sdk/ice-extensions, backed by the one ice-harness guard. Native C ABI cannot share a JS Symbol; preserve discoverability/version/method semantics with an explicit service ID and typed request/response. Do not load an external goal extension automatically.',
 'Goal extensions need a stable, narrow host seam instead of duplicating authority or verification.');
add(23,'Immutable Goals authority snapshot and session binding','P0',[70,140],
 ref(1303,1346)+'; '+ref(1445,1466)+'; '+src(host,6,15)+'. snapshotGoals/goalSessionIdentity, IceGoalsHostSnapshot. Tests: '+src(htest,179,224)+'; '+src(htest,299,324)+'.',
 'A goal extension can inspect current parent authority and verifier identity, bound to the actual native session object rather than a caller-supplied session ID.',
 'Require goalHostActive, initialized state, nonempty activeSessionId and activeSessionManager. Read ctx.sessionManager, its ID/file and ctx.cwd inside a try; any stale getter failure becomes "ICE Goals host context is stale.". Require both session-manager object identity and session ID to match captured active values. The returned saved boolean is sessionFile!==undefined; snapshot itself does not require saved or build. Read trust with stale error conversion.\n\nFreeze a copy of effective tool names, then freeze the snapshot {sessionId,mode,trusted,root,mutationGeneration,commandHash? ,tools,workgraphDispatch}. Include commandHash only when argv configured. workgraphDispatch is current scoped flag===true, independent of whether a Workgraph coordinator exists. The snapshot is an authority observation, not a capability to mutate mode or execute commands; it contains no argv or credentials.',
 quote(host,6,15)+'\nInput is native ExtensionContext, not model JSON. Output outer object and tools array are frozen. No setting/env/new slash/tool/keybinding or standalone file. Exact errors: no active session, stale context, no active guard state.',
 ['SAFE-002','SAFE-003','SAFE-004','SAFE-019','SAFE-022','SAFE-025'],
 'Rust supports execution-context snapshots scoped to plugin invocation (rust:crates/ice-extensions/src/actions.rs:586-614,1189-1220) and active-tool queries (400-405). It lacks the ICE root/mode/mutation/hash/workgraph snapshot and native-session-manager binding.',
 'Represent snapshot as an immutable serializable value in ice-harness; validate session generation/ownership before fulfilling plugin action. Do not accept session identity, trusted or effective tools from plugin JSON. Map the TS object-identity rule to an opaque host-owned session generation token.',
 'A goal consumer must not use a stale or forged authority snapshot from another session.');
add(24,'Goals fresh verification with overlap, cancellation and stale-pass rejection','P0',[140,250],
 ref(218,230)+'; '+ref(1328,1346)+'; '+ref(1406,1415)+'; '+ref(1468,1521)+'; '+src(host,17,34)+'. verifyGoals/isCurrentGoalVerification; IceGoalsHostVerification. Tests: '+src(htest,208,314)+'.',
 'A goal extension can request fresh verification of the already-configured command, with passing receipts rejected when authority or workspace generation changes during the run.',
 'Validate native session identity first, then initialized build mode, trusted project, saved session (session file is not undefined), configured argv, neither request nor context signal pre-aborted, approved-plan read acknowledgement when applicable, and no verifierRunning or activeGoalVerification. Fail by throwing, not returning a passing receipt. Record host-owned run {epoch,sessionId,root,generation,commandHash,active:true}; force the shared verifier even when checkedGeneration already equals current.\n\nA run is current only while active, host active, same epoch, state exists/build, same root/current generation, approved plan is read, same manager/ID and currently trusted. When not current, shared verify returns raw settled result without updating checkedGeneration or final verifier state. The Goals wrapper rechecks currentness after await; transform passed to stale if stale, else passed to cancelled if either signal aborted, otherwise preserve the actual status. Thus an already-failed stale run stays failed rather than becoming stale. Return captured session/root/generation, result hash falling back to captured hash, status and optional exitCode; omit logs/duration/argv. In finally deactivate the run and clear activeGoalVerification only by identity.\n\nCancellation is forwarded to the same active subprocess, not a second verifier. Shutdown invalidates before waiting so late passes cannot be accepted. A stale Goals completion can leave the persisted verifier status running until another verification/restore replaces it; do not claim every stale path writes a cancelled receipt. This guards observed mutation generations only, not unobserved shell/external edits.',
 quote(host,17,34)+'\nRequest accepts only optional AbortSignal. Status may be stale in addition to normal verifier statuses. Exact gates/errors are listed in mechanism; concurrent requests throw "ICE verification is already running." rather than join the active Promise. No env/setting/tool/CLI/keybinding/new arbitrary command API.',
 ['SAFE-003','SAFE-013','SAFE-019','SAFE-020','SAFE-021','SAFE-022','SAFE-023'],
 'Rust lifetime/cancellation primitives exist (rust:crates/ice-extensions/src/actions.rs:559-614,759-777,984-1019,1126-1163), but no Goals verification action combines native session identity, mode/trust, plan acknowledgement, generation and configured-command identity.',
 'Add one typed host action in ice-plugin-sdk backed by ice-harness verifier. Bind cancellation and receipt identity to the parent session token; reject overlapping calls explicitly. Do not expose arbitrary argv or trust overrides. File-content freshness is outside this generation receipt and must be separately checked by consumers.',
 'Without stale-pass rejection a goal consumer could accept evidence from a different workspace state.');
add(25,'Authoritative frozen capability publication to subagents','P0',[50,100],
 ref(790,806)+'; '+ref(895,907)+'; '+ref(942,981)+'; '+ref(1861,1879)+'; '+src('packages/coding-agent/src/ice.ts',86,97)+'; '+src('packages/coding-agent/src/ice.ts',118,124)+'. IceCapabilityState/IceSafeVerifyOptions/createIceSafeVerify. Tests: '+tests(382,407)+'.',
 'Subagent admission receives the parent guard’s current effective authority, rather than inferring permissions from UI mode text or independent configuration.',
 'After applying tools and persisting on restore/mode change, call optional onCapabilityChange with Object.freeze({mode,tools:Object.freeze([...effectiveTools(ctx)]),bashEnabledInRecordedProcess,allowExternal:effectiveExternal}) and ctx. The tool array is a new copy; both levels are frozen. The current launcher stores this value and mode in closure variables and provides getter callbacks to subagents. onModeChange is invoked after status/warnings; onCapabilityChange precedes it. Callbacks are awaited; thrown callback errors propagate rather than being logged and ignored. The snapshot is not automatically republished for every registry/trust change; effectiveTools at each tool_call still recomputes admission. Draft creation changes read_plan availability through applyTools but does not invoke publishCapabilityState in that path.',
 quote(main,790,806)+'\nNo model-facing command or serialized RPC type is added by these embedding callbacks. No environment variable/settings key/file. tools may contain legacy allowlist names not currently registered; downstream admission must reconcile actual tool availability.',
 ['SAFE-003','SAFE-004'],
 'Rust execution-context capture for live child invocations exists (rust:crates/ice-extensions/src/actions.rs:586-614,1126-1163), but it has no guard-owned mode/tool/Bash/external snapshot or callback bridge from the ICE launcher.',
 'Keep one immutable parent authority snapshot in ice-harness; inject it into child admission instead of a second permission controller. Native plugin host additions should pass opaque/copy-only capabilities. Determine whether registry/trust changes require extra publication in the Rust design; current TS publication points are limited as described.',
 'Children must never reconstruct broader authority than the parent guard granted.');
add(26,'Guard status reporting and safety notifications','P2',[50,100],
 ref(768,787)+'; '+ref(966,979)+'; '+ref(1590,1624)+'; '+ref(1865,1877)+'. report/verifierFailureMessage and /ice-status. Tests: '+tests(1143,1154)+'; '+tests(1166,1196)+'.',
 'Expose mode, root, current trust/opt-ins, plan state and verifier freshness without implying OS containment.',
 'The /ice-status handler is a no-op before state exists. Otherwise build the exact newline-separated fields below and report info through ctx.ui.notify. report additionally console.error only in print mode, keeping JSON/RPC stdout clean. Mode transitions and restore set status ice-mode and warn with sticky IDs safety:bash or safety:external when effective. These warn that direct path guards do not contain shell commands and external access is unrestricted host access, not a sandbox. Verifier completion updates ice-verify as specified by SAFE-021. Status is observational and does not force verification or mutate approval.',
 '| Output field, in order | Value/fallback |\n|---|---|\n| Mode | state.mode |\n| Guard root | state.guardRoot |\n| Root source | state.rootSource |\n| Project trusted | current trust boolean |\n| Bash requested / Bash effective | process request / trusted-build effective |\n| External access requested / External access effective | process request / trusted-build effective |\n| Plan status / Plan title | status / title or none |\n| Plan read in build | boolean |\n| Plan approval mode | policy or none |\n| Plan decision reminders | count |\n| Plan model before entry | reference or none |\n| Plan execution model | reference or default |\n| Mutation generation / Checked generation | counters |\n| Verifier configured | argv !== undefined |\n| Verifier status / Verifier generation | status / generation or none |\n| Latest exit code / Latest duration | value or none |\n| Output truncated | value or false |\n\nSlash /ice-status ignores args. No settings/env/keybinding/tool schema or new RPC command.',
 ['SAFE-003','SAFE-004','SAFE-021'],
 'Rust plugin SetStatus action and UI status ownership exist (rust:crates/ice-extensions/src/actions.rs:881-923,2008-2068), but no guard-specific status command, safety warnings or field formatting is registered.',
 'Implement formatting in ice-cli against the guard snapshot. Keep stderr/report-mode behavior separate from JSON/RPC stdout. Reuse native sticky notification/status mechanisms after the TUI host audit; do not rebrand the guard as a sandbox.',
 'Useful diagnostics, but not itself an authority-enforcement prerequisite.');
